{"title":"Tangential quadrilateral","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A tangential quadrilateral is a quadrilateral that has an incircle. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pitot_Theorem\" title=\"Pitot Theorem\">Pitot Theorem</a> states that in any sich quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/2418083aa7e970c341684e1060b29541ff4905f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB + CD= BC + AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"184\" height=\"14\" />.\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Tangential_quadrilateral&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017152603\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.005 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 13/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 361/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   19.130      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%   19.130      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31385:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017152603 and revision id 245982. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}